CONSENT CALENDAR  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

3.. Reaffirm adoption of Resolution No. 2021-61 finding a proclaimed state of emergency continues to impact the ability to meet safely in person, and allows meetings of the City Council and all City boards, commissions and committees to be conducted remotely as needed in compliance with new Brown Act provisions identified in Assembly Bill 361  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

4.. Adopt Resolution No. 2021-73 modifying the pay schedule for part-time, non-permanent and non-classified employees to comport with the State minimum wage increase effective January 1, 2022  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

5.. Authorization to Collaborate with the County of Orange and American Family Housing to Submit an Application for the Homekey Program Grant Funding Initiative  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

6.. Introduction of the Proposed Memorandum of Understanding Between the Management Employees’ Organization (MEO) and the City of Huntington Beach for January 1, 2022, through December 31, 2024  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 OC introduced 6, 7, 8 together. \par
\par
Brittany Mello gave the staff report for Items No. 6, 7, 8 with slides entitled: introduction of proposed memoranda of understanding with the management employees association, marine safety association, and police management association; overview; proposed memoranda of understanding; FY 2021/22 Fiscal Impact; FY 2022/23 Fiscal Impact; FY 2023/24 Fiscal Impact; City Council Options\par
\par
Oc thanked representatives from MEO, MSA, PMA. \par
\par
Carr- thanked mello for presentation and thanked labor representatives\par
\par
Posey- compliment all three labor groups for making their proposals easy to understand and negotiations prompt/smooth. Thanked Mello and Chi for making negotiations 2 1/2-3 years. Seems like we're in perpetual negotiation. Looking at shrinking labor pool. Want HB to attract the best and brightest. Staff is this councils #1 priority. \par
\par
Bolton- think each councilmember has seen how hard our staff works. Hope members of the public agree. Seen some suggestions that there's something wrong with the process and challenge anyone to deny providing appropriate pay. \par
\par
Delgleize- (see video)\par
\par
\par
}


7.. Introduction for the Proposed Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) Between the Huntington Beach Marine Safety Management Association (MSMA) and the City of Huntington Beach for January 1, 2022, through December 31, 2024  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

8.. Introduction of the Proposed Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) Between the Huntington Beach Police Management Association (PMA) and the City of Huntington Beach for July 1, 2021, through December 31, 2023  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Mike Posey

9.. Approve the appointment of Eric Parra to the position of Chief of Police and authorize the City Manager to execute the associated Employment Agreement.  -  Action: approved (Pass) Moved by Barbara Delgleize {\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0\deflang1033{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset0 Arial;}}
{\colortbl ;\red0\green0\blue0;}
\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\fs24 Chief Harvey- thank council for kind words and support. The city is in best possible position to bring Chief Para. He has impeccable credentials and experience. \par
\par
Chief Para- thanked council for the opportunity and a goal of continuous improvement and collaboration. Thanked Chief Harvey. Here for you, the community, and the PD\par
\par
Carr- echoed comments. Heartfelt thank you for Chief Harvey. You will be missed. Very excited to welcome Chief Para. This is a community and a council that will support you. \par
\par
OC- thanked Harvey for his work, reviewed recruitment process, 14 final candidates, 4 finalists who went through a very intensive process; including 2 panels with other police chiefs and one with city staff. 3 candidates were interviewed again before Para chosen.\par
\par
Reviewed contract.\par
\par
Posey- thanked Chief Harvey for his service and his communication with council. Will be missed. This was a tough decision. Grateful that Mr. Para applied. Welcome to City of HB\par
\par
Delgleize- welcome Chief Para. Thanked Chief Harvey- brought grace with him that was so appreciated. You made it easier for council to explain situations to the public. City has benefitted from your work here. Agree with Posey that there were great candidates.\par
\par
Moser- Thank Chief Harvey- echoed Delgleize's comments, thanked for transforming and leveling up the police department and being so responsive. Leave big shoes to fill. Look forward to partnering with Chief Para and building the trust with the department.\par
\par
kalmick- echo council's comment. Thank Harvey for his service and his knowledge, and filling the gap. Thank Chief Para for stepping up to serve your community. Appreciate energy professionalism and curiosity. \par
\par
bolton- Thank Chief Harvey for his open mindedness and innovation.\par
}


